<title>USA: W. House, Congress budget talks to resume Thursday.</title>
<headline>W. House, Congress budget talks to resume Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House spokesman Mike McCurry said on Thursday that budget negotiations between the White House and Congress were expected to resume on Thursday and may last much of the day.</p>
<p>&quot;They're going up some time this morning and then they anticipate being there probably most of the day,&quot; McCurry said, referring to White House negotiators going to Capitol Hill for talks on balancing the budget by 2002.</p>
</text>
